nd one Tossup", "Recent Democratic-sponsored poll shows Leonard tied, with outside groups attacking Carey", "National environment favors Democrats by several points"], "rationale": "The fundamentals still favor Carey: an R+5 seat, incumbency, and a big fundraising edge, and most expert ratings sit at Likely R. But the Democratic-leaning Hart poll from late September shows a tied race, outside spending has targeted Carey over SNAP and Medicaid cuts, and the favorable national environment narrows the expected margin to roughly three points Republican.", "watch": "Any independent polling confirming the Hart result, or further outside spending into the district, would move this toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Carey (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's 15th District leans Republican by about five points, and incumbent Mike Carey returns with a large financial advantage over Democratic challenger Don Leonard. Most nonpartisan raters still place the race at Likely Republican, though a couple have moved it to Lean Republican and one calls it a Tossup.\n\nThe race has tightened in recent months. A September poll from a Democratic-leaning firm showed the candidates essentially tied, and outside groups have spent against Carey, attacking his votes on SNAP, Medicaid, and education. A Libertarian candidate also appears on the ballot. The combination of a favorable national climate for Democrats and visible spending keeps the seat competitive, but Carey's incumbency, district lean, and money still make him the favorite heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1732, "margin": -5.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.185, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1905, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1541, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1527, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1532, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1445, "m